# Jugglebot repeated self-toss: throw -> catch -> dwell -> throw ... num_throws times,
# from ONE goal. The bridge between the validated single Toss and 2-ball juggling
# (single-ball-toss plan, Phase F). Hosted by the same ball-ops node as Reload and Toss
# (reload_coordinator_node) and covered by the SAME one-ball-op-at-a-time claim: a
# Reload or Toss goal while a session runs — or a session while either runs — is
# REJECTED_BUSY at accept, because all three actions own the hand, the catch/armed latch
# and the Teensy's last-writer-wins trajectory queue.
#
# It is a SEQUENCER, not a new capability. Every cycle is an ordinary Toss run by the
# same toss_sequencer FSM through the same coordinator code path, so every Toss
# precondition, abort ladder, arming order and terminal applies UNCHANGED per cycle. The
# session itself commands NO motion of its own: there is no session-level positioning
# move, no session-level go_home, no session-level hand dispatch. What it adds is (a)
# when the next cycle starts, (b) whether it starts at all, and (c) the per-cycle
# accounting the operator scores the sitting from.
#
# WHY IT NEEDS NO HAND MOVE BETWEEN CYCLES (the fact the design rests on): the firmware
# catch stroke ENDS at 0 rev (Trajectory.h buildCatch, xA = {x3, x5, x6, 0.f}) and a
# kind-0 throw stroke STARTS at 0 rev (buildThrow, xA = {0.f, x1, x2, x3}). The catch is
# its own re-park and the throw is its own catch-prime. Measured on the 2026-07-27
# sitting: hand pos_meas is within +-0.045 rev of park at the CAUGHT instant on all 17
# self-tosses, and its worst excursion over the following 3 s is 0.069 rev against the
# +-0.5 rev park band (7.2x margin) — so cycle N+1's REJECTED_HAND_NOT_PARKED gate
# passes with no intervening command.
#
# WHY THE PLATFORM NEEDS NO MOVE EITHER: a CAUGHT toss ends in ACTION_STAY (config
# jugglebot_operational.toss_stay_at_pose_on_caught, default true) and
# trajectory/commanded_position reports the live pose, so cycle N+1's throw site A is
# cycle N's catch pose for free. Since 2026-08-23 trajectory/commanded_pose reports the
# ORIENTATION of that same sample too, so cycle N+1 can also prove it is already at the
# pre-tilt pose and skip the zero-millimetre positioning move on an AIMED chain — worth
# 0.38 s of every cycle's throw delay, and the whole reason the cadence ladder stopped
# publishing a separate (slower) aimed column. See the KNOWN LIMITATION below.
#
# DWELL is defined as previous SCHEDULED LANDING -> next RELEASE, and it is realised as a
# QUIESCENT WAIT before the next cycle starts — never as a stretched throw_delay. That
# keeps every cycle's internal timing bit-identical to a validated single toss (the only
# timing the hardware ladder has ever measured), and it keeps the catch latch DOWN
# between cycles instead of leaving the reactive-catch path armed over a loaded cup.
#
# See plans/active/single-ball-toss.md Phase F and
# tests/hardware/session_anomaly_fixes.md SECTION CONT.

geometry_msgs/Point catch_position   # nominated catch point for EVERY cycle, mm,
                                     # STOW-relative platform frame (same convention as
                                     # Toss.action / TimedTarget.pose; z 170 = ACTIVE
                                     # plane). v1 is deliberately ONE point for the whole
                                     # session: a per-cycle waypoint list (A -> B -> C
                                     # with a different B each cycle) is the obvious v2
                                     # and is explicitly OUT OF SCOPE here — it needs the
                                     # throw-site frame question settled first (see the
                                     # KNOWN LIMITATION below), and a fixed B is the
                                     # well-conditioned case: measured, a fixed-B chain
                                     # CONVERGES (residual A-offset 3.017 mm at cycle 2,
                                     # 0.062 mm at cycle 3, 0.001 mm at cycle 4).
float64 throw_height_m               # apex height above the release plane (m), same for
                                     # every cycle; 0 => config default (~0.78 m apex).
                                     # Converted once to flight time T = sqrt(8*h/g).
int32 num_throws                     # how many toss-catch cycles to run. Must be in
                                     # [1, jugglebot_operational.toss_session_max_throws]
                                     # (20) or REJECTED_NUM_THROWS. num_throws = 1 is
                                     # exactly one Toss, with the session accounting.
float64 dwell_time_s                 # previous SCHEDULED LANDING -> next RELEASE (s);
                                     # 0 => config default toss_session_dwell_default_s.
                                     # FLOOR, and it is DERIVED not chosen:
                                     #   dwell >= max(throw_delay_s + handoff_margin_s,
                                     #               hand_stroke.min_turnaround_dwell_s)
                                     # because a cycle's release is its own accept +
                                     # throw_delay, and the session cannot start cycle N+1
                                     # before cycle N's possession verdict has landed AND
                                     # the hand is back inside the park band
                                     # (handoff_margin_s, 2026-08-22). At the 5.0 s default
                                     # throw delay that is 5.137 s. Below it =>
                                     # REJECTED_DWELL. A dwell the
                                     # machine cannot honour is never silently stretched
                                     # into a longer one — it is refused, because a
                                     # cadence that is quietly ignored is a lie about what
                                     # the machine did.
                                     # NOTE the ACHIEVED dwell after a MISSED cycle the
                                     # session continues past (stop_on_miss false) can be
                                     # LONGER than requested: that cycle's SAFE_ABORT
                                     # ladder retracts the hand and installs a 2.0 s
                                     # go_home, both on service acks, so the session waits
                                     # out a 2.80 s floor from the landing before starting
                                     # the next cycle. It is a FLOOR, never a shortening;
                                     # per_cycle_dwell_s reports what actually happened.
float64 throw_delay_s                # delay from goal-accept to the FIRST release (s);
                                     # 0 => the Toss default (5.0 s). Cycles 2..N use the
                                     # SAME internal delay, but their release instants are
                                     # set by dwell_time_s, so this field only moves the
                                     # first one. Must be >= toss_session.min_throw_delay_s
                                     # or REJECTED_THROW_DELAY — that gate is what makes
                                     # the absolute dwell floor above a real floor rather
                                     # than an arithmetic identity, and it names the field
                                     # the operator actually set wrong instead of letting
                                     # cycle 1 die REJECTED_CANT_MAKE_LEAD.
                                     #
                                     # The floor was a flat MIN_TOSS_THROW_DELAY_S = 3.5 s
                                     # until 2026-08-22 (operator decision 3), then the
                                     # DERIVED kind-0 dispatch budget, and since 2026-08-23
                                     # that budget PLUS the pre-dispatch sequence the
                                     # runtime guard measures it after: 0.361 s at the
                                     # 0.80 s default flight, 0.417 s at the C-HAND-3 band
                                     # floor. Charging the dispatch budget alone let a goal
                                     # be ACCEPTED and then abort ABORTED_CANT_MAKE_RELEASE
                                     # on every cycle, with the catch armed and the hand
                                     # committed.
                                     #
                                     # ONE cycle may be granted MORE than this field asks
                                     # for: the first cycle of a sitting has to COMMAND its
                                     # pre-positioning move (later cycles hold the pose
                                     # they threw from and take the census-B1 skip), which
                                     # costs 0.38 s more of lead. The coordinator raises
                                     # that cycle's delay and logs one WARN naming the
                                     # raise; the session's landing-anchored schedule
                                     # absorbs it and the CADENCE is unchanged. A single
                                     # Toss is refused instead — there the delay is an
                                     # appointment the operator set, not a cadence
                                     # parameter the session consumes.
float64 catch_vel_scale              # 0 => config default; same semantics and clamp
                                     # [0.3, 1.5] as Toss.action / Reload.action. Applies
                                     # to every cycle.
bool stop_on_miss true               # OPERATOR DECISION (c), 2026-07-28: default TRUE.
                                     # The IDL default above is LOAD-BEARING — an omitted
                                     # field must mean STOP, never CONTINUE. A missed
                                     # catch leaves a loose ball on the floor under a
                                     # machine that is about to stroke again, which is the
                                     # scenario this flag exists to prevent. Setting it
                                     # false is a BENCH affordance (the no-ball dry trace
                                     # needs it to reach cycle 3), never a session default.
                                     #
                                     # It governs the MISSED class only. A cycle that ends
                                     # REJECTED_* or ABORTED_* stops the session
                                     # REGARDLESS: that is a machine fault, and repeating a
                                     # fault num_throws times is how one fault becomes N.
                                     # ONE carve-out since 2026-08-11, and it is NOT a
                                     # relaxation: REJECTED_NO_BALL with on_empty_cup RELOAD
                                     # runs the reload interlude instead of stopping. That
                                     # terminal is the one where the FSM provably commanded
                                     # NOTHING (minted in CHECKING, before _positioned /
                                     # _prepare_dispatched, so _terminal_action is
                                     # ACTION_NONE), so the interlude is entered from a
                                     # provably quiescent machine.
string on_empty_cup "STOP"           # STOP (default) | RELOAD — what the session does when a
                                     # cycle is REJECTED_NO_BALL, i.e. the cup is empty
                                     # because the previous ball bounced out during the dwell
                                     # (the retention case stop_on_miss structurally cannot
                                     # see — see the S3 header above).
                                     # The IDL default is LOAD-BEARING and the node re-applies
                                     # it: ANY value that is not exactly "RELOAD" (empty,
                                     # misspelt, an older client's unset field) resolves to
                                     # STOP. An unreadable field must never start an
                                     # autonomous BB reload the operator did not ask for.
                                     # RELOAD is reachable under BOTH stop_on_miss settings,
                                     # and the PRIMARY route is stop_on_miss TRUE — the case
                                     # named two lines up. A CAUGHT cycle whose ball bounces
                                     # out during the dwell is not a MISS (the verdict was
                                     # minted at ARRIVAL and nothing re-verifies retention),
                                     # so stop_on_miss never sees it; the NEXT cycle finds an
                                     # empty cup and mints REJECTED_NO_BALL, and that is what
                                     # fires the interlude. With stop_on_miss FALSE there is
                                     # a second route: a MISSED cycle drops the ball, the
                                     # session continues, and the next cycle finds the cup
                                     # empty for the ordinary reason.
                                     # PREREQUISITE, checked LIVE at the interlude: config
                                     # jugglebot_operational.toss_require_ball_evidence must
                                     # be true. With it false a drop produces a silent empty
                                     # dry stroke and the session would "reload" around a
                                     # toss that never happened —
                                     # STOPPED_BALL_EVIDENCE_DISABLED.
int32 max_reloads                    # How many reload attempts the WHOLE session may spend.
                                     # 0 => config default
                                     # (jugglebot_operational.toss_session_max_reloads, 3).
                                     # Negative => REJECTED_BAD_GOAL(max_reloads), the same
                                     # sign-typo doctrine the other numerics carry.
                                     # This is the ONLY machine-side fence on ball supply:
                                     # ball_butler_node has no ball-count or magazine field,
                                     # so supply has NO machine observability and none is
                                     # invented here. On exhaustion the SESSION fails closed
                                     # with STOPPED_RELOAD_BUDGET; the capture tool treats
                                     # that terminal as "node exhausted" and skips the node.
---
bool success                         # True iff throws_completed == num_throws AND
                                     # catches_confirmed == num_throws (a clean session).
                                     # Note COMPLETED can carry success=False when
                                     # stop_on_miss is false and a cycle missed.
string outcome                       # COMPLETED | STOPPED_ON_MISS | REJECTED_<code> |
                                     # ABORTED_<code>. ABORTED_CYCLE_<cycle outcome>
                                     # carries the failing cycle's own verdict verbatim
                                     # (e.g. ABORTED_CYCLE_REJECTED_HAND_NOT_PARKED) so a
                                     # failure routes to the same place a single Toss
                                     # would have routed it.
int32 throws_completed               # cycles that got a ball into the air (CAUGHT or
                                     # MISSED). A cycle rejected before release does NOT
                                     # count.
int32 catches_confirmed              # cycles whose announced ball came back CAUGHT
                                     # (contract C-POSSESS-1's verdict — arrival-only; see
                                     # ros_ws/docs/ball_possession_contract.md).
string[] per_cycle_outcomes          # one Toss outcome string per STARTED cycle, in order
float64[] per_cycle_catch_error_mm   # per cycle, tracker last-KF horizontal miss (NaN
                                     # when not caught / unknown)
float64[] per_cycle_flight_s         # per cycle, measured release->catch-plane time (NaN
                                     # when unknown)
int32 reloads_used                   # reload attempts actually spent (<= the resolved
                                     # max_reloads). The session is the only witness of this
                                     # — the interlude runs under the session's own busy
                                     # claim, so no external Reload goal exists to count —
                                     # and the capture tool scores "node exhausted" from it.
float64[] per_cycle_dwell_s          # per cycle, the ACHIEVED landing(N-1) -> release(N)
                                     # spacing. NaN for cycle 1 (no previous landing).
                                     # This is the measurand the cadence row of the
                                     # hardware ladder scores: requested dwell is a target
                                     # the session never undershoots, and a cycle whose
                                     # cleanup ran long simply reports a longer one.
---
int32 cycle_index                    # 1-based index of the live cycle; 0 before the first
                                     # cycle starts
string phase                         # SESSION_CHECKING | DWELL, or the live cycle's Toss
                                     # phase verbatim (CHECKING | POSITIONING | PREPARING |
                                     # THROWING | BALL_IN_FLIGHT | CATCHING | SETTLING).
                                     # SESSION_CHECKING is published exactly ONCE, at goal
                                     # accept with cycle_index 0, BEFORE the session's own
                                     # CHECKING is adjudicated — so it appears even on a
                                     # session that is about to be REJECTED, which is
                                     # exactly when an operator wants to know the goal was
                                     # received rather than dropped.
int32 catches_confirmed              # running count, so a watched session is scoreable
                                     # live rather than only at the terminal
